        "content": "**Spring AI** is a Spring project for building AI-powered Java applications using familiar Spring patterns and abstractions.

### Key capabilities

- **Portable model APIs** for chat, embeddings, text-to-image, audio transcription, and moderation across providers such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Amazon Bedrock, Azure, and local models.
- **`ChatClient` fluent API** for sending prompts, configuring system/user messages, handling responses, and mapping output to Java types.
- **Tool calling** so models can invoke application functions or external services.
- **Structured output** to convert model responses into Java records, classes, or collections.
- **Prompt templates** and reusable prompt composition.
- **Conversation memory** for retaining context across interactions.
- **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** using document ingestion, embeddings, vector stores, and retrieval advisors.
- **Vector database integrations** including PostgreSQL/PGvector, Redis, Elasticsearch, MongoDB Atlas, Pinecone, Milvus, and others.
- **Spring Boot auto-configuration** and starters for model providers and vector stores.
- **Observability** through Spring’s metrics and tracing ecosystem.
- **MCP support** for integrating applications with Model Context Protocol clients and servers.

A minimal example looks like:

```java
@RestController
class AiController {

    private final ChatClient chatClient;

    AiController(ChatClient.Builder builder) {
        this.chatClient = builder.build();
    }

    @GetMapping("/ask")
    String ask(@RequestParam String question) {
        return chatClient.prompt()
                .user(question)
                .call()
                .content();
    }
}
```

You would also add the Spring AI starter for your chosen model provider and configure its API key in `application.properties` or `application.yml`.

Official documentation:

- [Spring AI reference documentation](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/)
- [Spring AI project page](https://spring.io/projects/spring-ai)
- [Getting Started guide](https://docs.spring.io/spring-ai/reference/getting-started.html)",
